# (#1361) the AOT's own matmul kernel (aot_tensor_matmul) leaves inf - inf as
# a raw NaN. The VM's builtin scans its result: strict raises "matmul: result
# is not a number", naming matmul, on the buffer and the list path alike.
# The soft halves are not printed here: the buffer NaN read (VM null, AOT 0)
# and a 1x1 list result's shape are older, separate divergences.
ab is buffer of 4
ab[0] is 1e300
ab[1] is 1e300
ab[2] is 1
ab[3] is 1
bb is buffer of 4
bb[0] is 1e300
bb[1] is 1
bb[2] is -1e300
bb[3] is 1
am is reshape of [ab, 2, 2]
bm is reshape of [bb, 2, 2]
try:
    r is matmul of [am, bm]
    print of r[3]
catch e:
    print of e.kind
    print of e.message
    print of e.line
la is [[1e300, 1e300], [1, 1]]
lb is [[1e300, 1], [-1e300, 1]]
try:
    lr is matmul of [la, lb]
    print of lr[1]
catch e:
    print of e.message
    print of e.line
ok is matmul of [[[1, 2], [3, 4]], [[1, 0], [0, 1]]]
print of ok
print of "after"
